--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -70,6 +70,41 @@ Run smart contract test with `yarn hardhat:test`
 - Edit your deployment scripts in `packages/hardhat/deploy`
 
 
+## USDC Staking
+
+This app lets people deposit USDC and withdraw it again at any time.
+
+- `packages/hardhat/contracts/Staker.sol` — holds the deposits. `stake(amount)` pulls USDC from the caller,
+  `withdraw(amount)` pays it back. No rewards, no lockup, no admin.
+- `packages/nextjs/app/stake` — the `/stake` page: wallet USDC, gas balance, staked position, and the
+  approve/stake/withdraw flow.
+
+The staked token is Circle's USDC on Base (`0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913`), configured per chain in
+`packages/hardhat/deploy/01_deploy_staker.ts` (contract side) and `packages/nextjs/contracts/externalContracts.ts`
+(frontend side).
+
+### Local development
+
+`yarn deploy` on a local chain also deploys `MockUSDC` — the same name, symbol and 6 decimals as the real token —
+and registers it as "USDC", so the page behaves exactly like it does on Base. Mint yourself a balance from the
+`Debug Contracts` page (`USDC` → `mint`), remembering the 6 decimals: 100 USDC is `100000000`.
+
+Two notes on `packages/nextjs/scaffold.config.ts`:
+
+- `targetNetworks` lists hardhat and Base. Drop hardhat for a production build.
+- Because that list is not local-only, the burner wallet is off (it would otherwise show up on Base). Temporarily
+  reduce `targetNetworks` to `[chains.hardhat]` if you want the burner wallet back while working locally.
+
+### Deploying to Base
+
+```
+yarn deploy --network base
+```
+
+That wires the Staker to the real USDC and regenerates `packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts`, which is
+what the frontend resolves the Staker address from. Set `NEXT_PUBLIC_ALCHEMY_API_KEY` (or an entry in `rpcOverrides`)
+before going live: the default RPC key is shared by every Scaffold-ETH app.
+
 ## Documentation
 
 Visit our [docs](https://docs.scaffoldeth.io) to learn how to start building with Scaffold-ETH 2.
